A||||5||Raydar||Have power windows. Adding power locks?||||5||
Z||000000||Raydar||05-16-2001||03:12 PM||||Did a search and found  a little bit of info.<BR>Need just a bit more.<BR>I understand that power windows and locks are in the same door harness. Is <I>all</I> of the wiring I need already there? Even under the dash?<BR>In order to add power locks to my power window doors, do I just need the buttons, actuators, and relay? <BR>How much of a PITA is it to install the actuators?<P>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 Duke coupe <BR>88 "wadded up" Formula (parts car)||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||05-16-2001||03:47 PM||||Its not too bad, just don't butcher the harnesses.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.michiganfieroclub.org" TARGET=_blank>http://www.michiganfieroclub.org</A>  has a good write-up about this procedure.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||05-16-2001||04:00 PM||||I can't tell you how much of a PITA it is to install the actuators but I can tell you that it is a one piece harness. Aside from the harness and actuators, you'll probably need the steel lock rods and actuator pivot.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||6
Z||000003||tgowens||05-16-2001||04:05 PM||||Roy is right - it's a one piece harness that runs from door to door and also down the center console.........that's the one you need......<P>------------------<BR>My Fiero Web Site.....<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tgowens.gif">             </A><P>87 GT - 2.8l Gold automatic<BR>87 GT - 2.8l Blue automatic<BR>87 GT - 3.4L Blue 5-speed Getrag<BR>87 GT - 2.8L Med. Red Met. 5-speed Getrag<BR>88 Coupe - 2.5L Red automatic||||reg||1
Z||000004||cadaver||05-16-2001||05:44 PM||||But No I dont think your car already has it. I have done many of these and other upgrades. You car can have locks or windows without having the other wiring. But when you strip out the donor car of the cross-car wiring harness it will have both. Then just remove your harness and replace it.<BR>The actuators are held in with big pop rivets. Just use 1/2 bolts and lock nuts and you will be good.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroJoe||05-16-2001||09:41 PM||||Also, make sure you are getting a cross car harness from a year that has the 3rd brake light if yours does too.  I've got an 87 Coupe, and the first harness I got with the power windows and locks had two totally different connectors that plug into other harnesses way up under the dash (by the "White box" power distribution thing)<P>The actuators werent hard at all.  I just used 1/4-20 x 1/2" hex bolts and lock nuts.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
